osp|n|The organ of hearing; the external ear. ; The sense of hearing; the perception of sounds; the power of discriminating between different tones; as, a nice ear for music; -- in the singular only. ; That which resembles in shape or position the ear of an animal; any prominence or projection on an object, -- usually one for support or attachment; a lug; a handle; as, the ears of a tub, a skillet, or dish. The ears of a boat are outside kneepieces near the bow. See Illust. of Bell. ; Same as Acroterium. ; Same as Crossette. ; Privilege of being kindly heard; favor; attention. ; The spike or head of any cereal (as, wheat, rye, barley, Indian corn, etc.), containing the kernels.	a:270j,96,6;1hg8,61,16;11tx,46,4~1hg8,61,16;270j,96,6;11tx,46,4	v:1a7k,53,1~1a7k,53,1	N:adf,124,3;1osd,103,3;22yd,82,18;1nv4,54,4;1ngf,42,2~22yd,82,18;1nv4,54,4;1osd,103,3;adf,124,3;1ngf,42,2
